# The space of node is lexical by the code, not by the data the launch was given (the author's decision 2026-11-11
# through fable2, plan M11 5b part 2): Bump launched over D reads D's hits, 100, by the bare name and writes the field of
# its own parent, the root, through node -- the root's hits is 101, D's stays 100.
int: hits 4
D: (int: hits 100)
Bump: (node\hits := hits + 1)
call(D; Bump)
int: seen hits
int: kept D\hits
